error[V0001]: this `User` is made right here, but this call needs a `User` stored in a name, because its result is part of it; store it with `let` first, then use that
  --> crates/varyk/tests/fixtures/errors/v0001_rooted_argument_made_right_there/main.vr:16:20
   |
16 |     println!("{}", make().name_ref());
   |                    ^^^^^^ this `User` is made right here, but this call needs a `User` stored in a name, because its result is part of it; store it with `let` first, then use that
   |
   = note: in Rust terms, the result is a reference into the value the call is made on, and Varyk only lets it point into a value stored in a `let`, not into a temporary one
